dnevnik-kuznetsa-name = blacksmith's diary
dnevnik-kuznetsa-desc = A heavy volume of cracked, scaly leather, smelling of sulfur and soot. The edges of the yellowed pages are charred and marked with old brown stains. The handwriting is angular, harsh, and pressed deep into the parchment.
dnevnik-kuznetsa-content = [color=#b22222][bold]Entry 73. Cycle of the Boiling Stone.[/bold][/color]


    {"The flame roars today like an awakened dragon. Perfect. Those cowardly beardlings on the surface, with their miserable coal furnaces, will never understand the true might of a volcano. They fear magma, worship it from afar. I have made it my anvil."}


    {"Finished reforging the elven breastplate. Filthy alloy, too much flexibility, the metal bends like a willow branch. No endurance at all against a heavy axe. I had to burn that soft-bellied filth out of the steel with acid. Surface folk forever glue shiny trinkets together and call them armor. Mahal would turn away from such disgrace. It is shame, not craft."}


    {"[color=#b22222][bold]Entry 74.[/bold][/color]"}


    {"My pick struck a new vein deep beneath the caldera, where even the stones groan from the underworld heat. The ore is black as the deepest cavern beneath the Lonely Mountain, and it rings under steel like an ancient temple bell."}

    {"[color=#555555]░▒▓[/color] Acrid sulfur smoke burned my lungs when I broke off the first piece. I laid the shard upon the altar-anvil. The warding runes upon it flared [color=#ff4500]crimson[/color]. Tomorrow I will cast this piece into the very throat of the forge."}


    {"[color=#b22222][bold]Entry 75.[/bold][/color]"}


    {"The stone will not melt. For three hours I worked the bellows until I nearly boiled in my own boots. The magma seethed, hot enough that common iron would have run like water, yet this black ore only reddened a little!"}

    {"I had to add powder from the fire glands of a cave salamander. [color=#333333]██▓▒░[/color] A spray of sparks leapt straight into my beard! Barely put it out. But the metal finally yielded. Strike it with the heavy hammer, and the sound is as if the mountain itself answers with a dull groan. I will forge an axe from this, worthy of the forefathers. Our Uzbad will pay generously for such a weapon."}


    {"[color=#b22222][bold]Entry 76.[/bold][/color]"}


    {"At night, the iron gate on the lower levels burst. Blind cave things crawled again toward the warmth of the forge. I had to drop the tongs and take up the old axe. [bold]Baruk Khazad! Khazad ai-menu![/bold] Their foul blood hissed into steam upon the red-hot floor stones."}

    {"[color=#8b0000]▓▒░██░▒▓[/color] One thing crept too close. Tore my thigh open with a claw. The wound is deep. I barely bound my leg with a tourniquet before I bled out beside the forge. [color=#8b0000]▒▓███[/color]"}


    {"[bold]Tasks for the week:[/bold]"}

    {"- Clear soot from the air pipes (the draft is weakening, the bellows creak)."}

    {"- Sharpen the dulled picks and replace the hafts."}

    {"- Forge twin blades for [color=#8b0000]▓██▒░[/color]"}

    {"- Reinforce the lower gate with extra beams."}


    {"[bold]By Mahal's anvil and Durin's beard, if this black ore does not yield to my hammer by week's end, I will make the mountain itself spit it back out![/bold][color=#333333]▓▓████...[/color]"}

zalityy-krovyu-sudovoy-zhurnal-name = blood-soaked ship's log
zalityy-krovyu-sudovoy-zhurnal-content = [head=3][color=#daa520]EXPEDITION REPORT: "GOLDEN SHORE"[/color][/head]


    {"[italic]Day One. Landing and establishing camp.[/italic]"}

    {"To the glory of the Trade Guild, our expedition has succeeded! We entered a splendid, quiet bay in longboats, landed directly upon the shore, and immediately began setting camp among the ruins of some ancient stone foundation. Our carpenters hastily built wooden barricades between the old walls. The stores are already filling with barrels of fresh water and crates of provisions. The natives still keep to the shadows of the jungle. They look like utter savages, yet they are magnificently built. I am certain our mirrors, beads, and iron axes will persuade them to surrender every treasure of this island. The profit promises to be colossal!"}


    {"[italic]Day Eight. Difficulties in negotiation.[/italic]"}

    {"I hasten to note the extreme strangeness of local customs. The savages have at last emerged from the thickets, but commerce proceeds abominably. They are wholly indifferent to our silks and ringing coin. Yesterday they brought baskets of strange, sweet-smelling meat as a gift, and in return... in return they merely stared intently at our sailors, felt their forearms, and clicked their tongues approvingly."}

    {"Last night our accountant Gustav vanished without a trace after going behind the ruined stone slabs to relieve himself. The guard at the flimsy gate has been doubled. Uneasy."}


    {"[italic]Day Fourteen. [color=#8b0000]CATASTROPHE[/color][/italic]"}

    {"[bold]They did not come for goods. WE ARE THEIR GOODS! WE ARE THEIR PROVISIONS![/bold]"}

    {"At dawn they poured out of the jungle like a swarm of locusts. Our pitiful wooden gates did not last a minute. These are not men, but primeval demons! They took no prisoners for ransom. With my own eyes I saw the boatswain dragged into the undergrowth while they tore pieces of flesh from him as they ran!"}

    {"My hands are shaking. I have wedged myself into a corner among the mossy stones, hidden behind empty crates. Right before me, our gold, the pride of the Guild, lies in the thick grass mixed with blood and mud. They do not need it."}

    {"They wander the ruins close by. I hear branches cracking under their feet, and I hear them sniffing. [color=#8b0000]They are throwing the crates aside. Their teeth are filed sharp, like the fangs of do██████▓▓▓▒▒▒░░░[/color]"}

